    "version" : "Version 0.1.0 DRAFT",
    "author" : [ "Nader Jelassi", "Marc-Andree Wolf" ],
    "description" : {
      "en" : "The four metals whose recycled content Regulation (EU) 2023/1542, Art. 8(1) requires a battery to declare: cobalt, lead, lithium and nickel. Declared as individuals of the cross-sectoral class dpp:MaterialType and used as the value set of eudpp:hasMaterialType on a eudpp:MaterialOfComposition, so that a recycled-content figure can be attributed to a named metal. Corresponds to BatteryPass-Ready Data Attribute Long List v1.3, attributes 48 to 54."
    },
    "labels" : {
      "en" : "EU DPP Battery Metals Vocabulary"
    },
    "comments" : {
      "en" : "Developed against the CIRPASS-2 CORE ontology v2.0.5 (refresh of 25 August 2026; P_DPP v2.0.6 of 27 August 2026, MAT v1.0.2). To be revisited when MAT v2 lands (ontologies-core#24, #25): #25 introduces eudpp:materialTypeScheme, to be added to these four concepts as it is to the ten chemistries, and recycledContentType, which splits pre- from post-consumer shares."
    },
